  VALUES
    ('ios_crash_gate', 'iOS crash gate', 'blocked', 'Authenticated App Store Connect confirms one iOS 1.0.1 crash on 2026-08-25, but privacy suppression exposes no device, OS, crash report, stack, or UUID. Current product commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 inherits the preventive storage-failure hardening and adds tolerant optional Open-Meteo decoding. Twelve targeted current-source iOS Simulator mapping/service tests pass, but they cannot identify or be attributed to the historical crash. Hosted run 33297505825 and evidence-head run 33299592101 passed only for predecessor authority 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6 and are non-transferable. Diagnostic access and symbolication, a complete current-source hosted run, an exact signed physical iPhone/iPad pass, and post-rollout crash evidence remain missing.', 'Obtain any diagnostic report Apple later exposes, symbolicate if available, run exact signed physical iPhone QA, and collect post-rollout evidence'),
    ('open_meteo_promotion_clearance', 'Open-Meteo promotion clearance', 'pass', 'The complete authenticated Gmail record was checked read-only on 2026-08-29. The 06:05:07 +05:00 request described Nimbo as free and non-monetized, with no subscriptions, advertising, paid features, affiliate links, accounts, analytics SDK, or sale of user data, and limited promotion to unpaid localized posts, one personalized contact plus at most one follow-up, genuine Apple/Google editorial submissions, and ordinary unpaid links. At 17:25 +05:00, Nicoletta Addimando via OpenMeteo GmbH replied in ticket 234272 and explicitly confirmed that under those terms Nimbo is entitled to use the non-commercial API. This pass is limited to that exact scope and the published Free API limits; monetization, paid promotion, attribution removal, limit changes, or other material facts require a new licensing decision.', 'Preserve the confirmed scope and reopen licensing review before any material monetization, promotion, attribution, endpoint, or usage-limit change'),
    ('release_artifact_source_sync', 'Release artifact source sync', 'blocked', 'Product/build-input commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 resolves to Android phone 1.1.0 (8), Wear OS 1.1.0 (1000008), and Apple 1.1.0 (6). It inherits the deterministic hosted UI harness, API 24 desugaring, fail-closed source-revision plumbing, bundle-specific Apple profiles, non-upload export contract, and pinned dependency graph from predecessor 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6. It additionally tolerates omitted optional forecast/AQI arrays while keeping required weather/time inputs fail-closed; 14 targeted Android-host and 12 targeted iOS Simulator tests pass, including cache and timezone preservation after rejected required-row responses. Runs 33297505825 and 33299592101 are green predecessor evidence and do not transfer; the complete hosted matrix for 2cdd438 is pending the next push. The protected release-signing environment contains 4/8 inputs; the two Android passwords, Apple P12, and its transport password remain absent behind the locked local Keychain, and the candidate workflow has not run. The schema-v2 manifest keeps all current artifact hashes and signing/physical evidence null; 0/3 artifacts are byte-verified and the gate remains blocked.', 'Unlock the local login Keychain, provision the four remaining protected release-signing secrets, run the master-only hosted workflow, promote its verified receipt, and bind exact physical QA to the retained bytes'),
    ('android_physical_smoke', 'Android device smoke', 'blocked', 'Historical product commit 9c2dce4200dbba5487c8c458ade4616005fde6e6 retains physical API 25 phone and API 24/API 36 emulator regression evidence, while predecessor authority 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6 has green hosted API 24/API 36 phone/tablet UI evidence. Neither transfers to current authority 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652, which changes shared provider decoding. Fourteen current-source Android-host service, mapping, and cache-preservation tests pass, but the complete current hosted UI matrix, upload-signed phone rerun, physical tablet/widget result, and paired physical Wear OS result are missing. The gate remains blocked.', 'Sign and verify phone vc8, then run the exact signed artifact on phone and tablet plus widget and paired Wear OS paths'),
    ('ios_physical_smoke', 'iOS physical smoke', 'blocked', 'Historical product commit 9c2dce4200dbba5487c8c458ade4616005fde6e6 retains simulator-only Apple 1.1.0 (6) app/widget/watch and localized creative evidence. Hosted iOS run 33297505825 and evidence-head run 33299592101 passed only for predecessor authority 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6. Current authority 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 changes shared provider decoding and has twelve targeted iOS Simulator service/mapping tests green, but no complete current hosted Apple surface/application run, distribution-signed archive or IPA, iOS 15 runtime pass, or physical iPhone/iPad/widget/paired-watch result. The gate remains blocked.', 'Create and verify distribution-signed build 6, re-establish CoreDevice readiness, then run the exact artifact on iPhone, iPad, widget, and paired watch paths'),
    ('domain_activation', 'Domain activation', 'pass', 'At 2026-08-29 10:40–10:41 +05:00, authenticated GitHub Pages settings showed DNS check successful and Enforce HTTPS enabled. The Let''s Encrypt certificate has CN nimbo.uz, SANs nimbo.uz/www.nimbo.uz, and validates for both hosts. WHOIS, .uz delegation, authoritative Cloudflare records, and independent 1.1.1.1/8.8.8.8 resolution pass. HTTPS returns 200 with verification result 0 for all 12 published UZ-root/RU/EN landing, press, privacy, and support routes plus growth, robots, sitemap, and the valid metadata schema. HTTP apex redirects to HTTPS; HTTP www reaches HTTPS apex in two redirects; HTTPS www redirects directly to HTTPS apex. All 12 localized HTML routes have the expected HTTPS canonical and language. Uzbek intentionally uses ' || chr(47) || ' rather than a separate ' || chr(47) || 'uz' || chr(47) || ' route.', 'Maintain dated DNS, certificate, redirect, canonical, and localized-route verification at each release'),
    ('store_policy_console_clearance', 'Store policy console clearance', 'pass', 'The 2026-08-28 App Store read-only check found no open review/compliance action. Google Play reported no policy issues at 2026-08-29 13:12 +05:00; production remained active at 1.0.2 (6), 100%. At 13:59:40 +05:00, UZ Custom Store Listing 4834799756935529888 was saved only as Draft, not submitted for review or published; Publishing overview still showed the latest publication on 2026-08-27. This is point-in-time Console evidence, not a guarantee against later review. See growth/quality/store-policy-console-2026-08-28.md and growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-29.md.', 'Re-check both app-global store policy surfaces at the next evidence cutoff')
) AS gates(gate_id, gate, status, evidence, next_action);
